<<~ ahu slot=`#/b5-browser-twins-collision-2026-10-31`>>

! b5-browser-twins collision (Anvil-Five: Lares (Tasked Spirit)) 2026-10-31

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/new-findings`>>

!! New findings
N1 [CONFIRMED by read, fails closed->repeats] Browser catalog re-found never repairs the pointer. open-browser-vessel.ts 1090-1099: the `bootKeys.catalogUrl` branch calls loadFoundedCatalogOrWarn(...blankCatalog) and sets NO bootKeyWrites.catalogUrl (only the else branch does). After one DATA-AMNESIA re-found, the stale pointer stays in IDB keystore "catalog-url"; every later boot re-founds a fresh blank (new url each time), so wikis registered after the re-found orphan on the next boot. Red: boot with catalogUrl naming a missing doc, boot twice, assert the second boot does not warn.
N2 F1 reach is narrower than reported: bites only when admit.hearthGatePubKey is non-null and (kind anchor, or kind charter). A null gate key resolves to own on both boots (no bug).
N3 F1 also leaves hearthCanonDocs baked with the admit boot's nexusPubkey (746, admittedCanonDocs) while later boots key everything else on the own island.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/findings`>>

!! Findings
F1 CONFIRMED. Writer 729-747 omits hearthIslandKind/Scope (bootstrap type 140-170 has no field). Reader 619-623: anchorGateKey null hard-coded, explicitScope only from walk. admit rides one boot (lararium-web main.ts 215-221 takeStashedAdmit removes the sessionStorage entry; pendingAdmit is module-level, so a same-tab non-reload reboot masks it; a reload exposes it). nexusIslandsBelow (mesh nexus-identity.ts 290) is empty at the own island, so carryPersonaKelUpTheGradient finds nothing; gate throws at 1249-1251. No other restore: grep of the browser package finds no island row, fleet board or holder path; node restores via nodeNexusStandsAt 55-84 (hearthPin.gatePubKey/islandScope). No test reboots after an admit: leaf-continuity.mjs founds offline then reloads (never admits); two-tab-walk.mjs admit path is the old paste flow; wire-vessel-rig halts at catalog-ready. Fails closed (boot halts, no leak). Red: wire-vessel-rig boot with admit (hearthGatePubKey set, kind anchor) to bootstrap-kept, then boot again with no admit; assert same nexusPubkey / no "absent" throw. Control: null-gate admit and founded leaf keep own key.
F2 CONFIRMED. Browser 1539-1552 `if (active)` on WikiActivationResult object (mesh wiki-activation.ts 45-47), always truthy; node 3209 reads active.ok. Failed activation flips activeSurfaceId, places open-wiki. Fails open in UI state only. No test touches the browser handler. Red: stub ensureActive -> {ok:false}; assert activeSurfaceId unchanged, no placeVerb.
F3 NARROWED. Divergence real (browser: no repo.flush before writeBootKeys at loadGenesis; automerge-repo saveDebounceRate defaults 100ms, so a window exists). But the window is the first boot only, when the catalog holds one self-record, so "orphans every registered wiki" overstates; the real cost is N1. Policy fork stays NEEDS-RULING; cheap cure inside the browser adapter: await repo.flush() before writeBootKeys (no collapse needed).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/net-collapse-re-measure`>>

!! Net collapse re-measure
Code-line counts reproduce within ~10% (browser spans 26/16/71/32/16/22/16/73/76; node 9/20/66/25/19/28/20/39). Glue deleted ~480-525 confirmed; the 180-200 add-back is an unwritten-code estimate, and omits per-vessel port adapters. Range -200..-400; "~330" is a plausible point, not a measurement. "800 touched" holds.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/verdicts`>>

!! Verdicts
Agree with all reporter verdicts and leans. Order: F1 red + N1 red first (both browser-only, no node collision). C1 should land F1 cure before or with the stage; old shape (bootstrap lacking island pair) refuses by name, no back-compat read.

<<~/ahu>>

